      "locked": false,
      "text": "Summary\n\nBlock (0, 0) is responsible for one 2x2 portion of C. To fill it, it needs\nfour pieces: A1 and A2 from A, B1 and B2 from B.\n\nFirst, A1 and B1 are loaded into the block's shared memory, and the threads\ncompute with them. Then the shared memory is overwritten with\nA2 and B2, and the threads compute again, adding the same running\ntotals.\n\nAfter that, the threads have everything they need, and each one writes its spot \nof C.\n\nEvery block does the same for every portion of C, with its own pieces,\nat the same time.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "Summary\n\nBlock (0, 0) is responsible for one 2x2 portion of C. To fill it, it needs\nfour pieces: A1 and A2 from A, B1 and B2 from B.\n\nFirst, A1 and B1 are loaded into the block's shared memory, and the threads\ncompute with them. Then the shared memory is overwritten with\nA2 and B2, and the threads compute again, adding the same running\ntotals.\n\nAfter that, the threads have everything they need, and each one writes its spot \nof C.\n\nEvery block does the same for every portion of C, with its own pieces,\nat the same time.",
